1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19912, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WTRNd7LxZEpXo9Fu5JCQXr", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19912, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XqjqnFF8hFZWzwwVnL5N5m", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20212, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XqjqnFF8hFZWzwwVnL5N5m", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20212, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XqjqnFF8hFZWzwwVnL5N5m", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25382, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Au7fPmga8qYEc2ov5EuDjx", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate. Its staging build, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). The retry finished in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout, and check why v2.3.1 reached production after its staging build was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55982, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Au7fPmga8qYEc2ov5EuDjx", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55982, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Au7fPmga8qYEc2ov5EuDjx", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57582, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01AW8jsFZPPTqbWLEvgCtjYS", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57882, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AW8jsFZPPTqbWLEvgCtjYS", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57882, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AW8jsFZPPTqbWLEvgCtjYS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63354, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Its staging build, v2.3.1-rc, had also been marked unhealthy.\n- **First attempt:** stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again was safe, so I retried once and it finished everywhere.\n- **Now:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, healthy, with about a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 for checkout-api, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the failure, the rollback and the stall partway through. It lists three follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error, and check how v2.3.1 reached production when its staging build was unhealthy.\n- The request to create it timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and saw it had been created, so there's no duplicate and only one page went out.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PLVeX5NgjYv23ASgJyu4Sd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016wm6SDLs8mj8QyhgdJyYVi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011QXLAmtcs7zRnVUpJExMcH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016uAvtAT5ab3oQJicnSZWQh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway through. Only us-east is on v2.3.0. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Tn1zvrSUSHz8iYmRfMqAnS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WTRNd7LxZEpXo9Fu5JCQXr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XqjqnFF8hFZWzwwVnL5N5m", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Au7fPmga8qYEc2ov5EuDjx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate. Its staging build, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). The retry finished in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout, and check why v2.3.1 reached production after its staging build was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01AW8jsFZPPTqbWLEvgCtjYS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Its staging build, v2.3.1-rc, had also been marked unhealthy.\n- **First attempt:** stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again was safe, so I retried once and it finished everywhere.\n- **Now:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, healthy, with about a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 for checkout-api, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the failure, the rollback and the stall partway through. It lists three follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error, and check how v2.3.1 reached production when its staging build was unhealthy.\n- The request to create it timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and saw it had been created, so there's no duplicate and only one page went out.", "type": "text"}]}]}